# Venv Usage — Single Source of Truth

**Conflict resolved:** Quality gates and tests use per-repo `.venv`. IDE and general Python use `.venv-workspace`. Never mix.

## Rule Matrix

| Task | Venv | Command | Why |
|------|------|---------|-----|
| **Quality gates** | Repo `.venv` | `cd <repo> && bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` | Script creates/sources `.venv`; CI-faithful |
| **pytest** | NEVER direct | Use `quality-gates.sh` only | Direct pytest uses wrong venv (workspace) |
| **IDE / IntelliSense** | Workspace `.venv-workspace` | pyrightconfig.json, Pylance | Cross-repo imports |
| **General Python** (scripts, lint outside QG) | Workspace when in session | `source .venv-workspace/bin/activate` | Convenience; not for tests |
| **Sub-agent** (isolated VM) | Repo `.venv` | `cd <repo> && bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` | No workspace venv; script handles it |

## DO

- **Tests:** `cd <repo> && bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` — no manual activation
- **Sub-agents:** Pass "For quality gates: cd <repo> && bash scripts/quality-gates.sh. Never .venv-workspace for pytest."
- **Workspace path:** Use `$UNIFIED_TRADING_WORKSPACE_ROOT` or `${workspaceFolder}` — never hardcode user paths

## NEVER

- Run `pytest` or `python -m pytest` directly (uses workspace venv → wrong)
- Tell sub-agents to "source .venv-workspace" before running quality-gates.sh
- Hardcode `/Users/.../Documents/` or `/Users/.../Code/` in configs

## Fallback (workspace-venv-fallback.mdc)

When repo `.venv` is broken (missing deps, wrong Python): use workspace venv as **debug workaround** only. Fix repo venv before merging. CI always uses fresh repo install.

